/-!
# Theorem 7 (Ch. III §7, p. 253): the initial forms of a normalized standard base

> THEOREM 7. Let R be a regular local ring, J an ideal in R and (S; z₁, …, z_r) a regular z-frame of R
> for J. [...] If (f₁, …, f_m) is a normalized standard base of J with respect to (S; z₁, …, z_r), then
> for every a (1 ≤ a ≤ t) the initial forms of f₁, …, f_{m_a} in gr_M(R) are all contained in the
> k-subalgebra of gr_M(R) generated by the initial forms of z₁, …, z_{τ_a} in gr_M(R). (p. 253)

The proof begins "First of all, R may be assumed to be complete with respect to the topology defined by
the powers of (z₁, …, z_r)R. (Namely, the proof in the general case can be easily reduced to this
special case.) Hence R = S{z₁, …, z_r}."  The reduction is carried out here, as in the proofs of Lemma 18
(`Ch3/FramePermissibleCenters.lean`) and Theorem 8 (`Compat/NormalizedStrictTransform.lean`): the base
change of §8 for `id : S → S`.  The complete case, the induction on `a` with the partial frames
`S_a = S{z_{τ_a+1}, …, z_r}` and Lemma 19, is
`initialForm_mem_adjoin_of_isNormalizedStandardBase_mvPowerSeries`
(`Compat/NormalizedStrictTransformComplete.lean`), which Theorem 8 uses.
-/

@[expose] public section

open IsLocalRing

namespace Hironaka

universe u

section Theorem7

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsRegularLocalRing R]

/-- Theorem 7, p. 253: "Let `R` be a regular local ring, `J` an ideal in `R` and
`(S; z₁, …, z_r)` a regular `τ`-frame of `R` for `J`. Let `t = t(J)`, so that
`r = τ^{(t)}(J)`. Let `τ_a = τ^{(a)}(J)` for `1 ≤ a ≤ t`. Let `m_a` be the maximal integer
such that `ν^{(m_a)}(J) = μ^{(a)}(J)` for `1 ≤ a ≤ t`. If `(f₁, …, f_m)` is a normalized
standard base of `J` with respect to `(S; z₁, …, z_r)`, then for every `a` (`1 ≤ a ≤ t`) the
initial forms of `f₁, …, f_{m_a}` in `gr_M(R)` are all contained in the `k`-subalgebra of
`gr_M(R)` generated by the initial forms of `z₁, …, z_{τ_a}` in `gr_M(R)`, where `M` denotes
the maximal ideal of `R` and `k = R/M`."

(Formalization note: `z₁, …, z_{τ_a}` are the `z_j` with `j < τ^{(a)}(J)`, indexed by the
subtype `{j : Fin r // (j : ℕ) < tau R J a}` rather than by a cast, as in
`IsRegularSystemOfTauParameters`.)

Printed route: "First of all, `R` may be assumed to be complete with respect to
the topology defined by the powers of `(z₁, …, z_r)R`": the base change of §8 for the identity
`S → S` (`RegularFrame.baseChangeHom`, `R̂ = S⟦z⟧`), the hypotheses transferring and the conclusion
descending (`initialForm_mem_framePrefixSubalgebra_of_map`); the induction on `a` for the complete
`R = S⟦z⟧`, with the partial frames `(S_a; z₁, …, z_{τ_a})` and Lemma 19, is
`initialForm_mem_adjoin_of_isNormalizedStandardBase_mvPowerSeries`
(`Compat/NormalizedStrictTransformComplete.lean`). -/

@[blueprint "thm:III.7"
  (statement := /-- Let $R$ be a regular local ring, $J$ an ideal in $R$ and
    $(S;z_1,\dots,z_r)$ a regular $\tau$-frame of $R$ for $J$ (\cref{def:III.10}). Let
    $t=t(J)$, so that $r=\tau^{(t)}(J)$. Let $\tau_a=\tau^{(a)}(J)$ for $1\le a\le t$. Let
    $m_a$ be the maximal integer such that $\nu^{(m_a)}(J)=\mu^{(a)}(J)$ for $1\le a\le t$
    (\cref{def:III.1}, \cref{def:III.6-mu}). If $(f_1,\dots,f_m)$ is a normalized standard
    base of $J$ with respect to $(S;z_1,\dots,z_r)$
    (\cref{def:III.9-normalized-standard-base}), then for every $a$ $(1\le a\le t)$ the
    initial forms of $f_1,\dots,f_{m_a}$ in $\operatorname{gr}_M(R)$ are all contained in the
    $k$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{gr}_M(R)$ generated by the initial forms of
    $z_1,\dots,z_{\tau_a}$ in $\operatorname{gr}_M(R)$, where $M$ denotes the maximal ideal of
    $R$ and $k=R/M$. (Theorem 7, p.~253.) -/)
  (proof := /-- First of all, $R$ may be assumed to be complete with respect to the topology
    defined by the powers of $(z_1,\dots,z_r)R$. (Namely, the proof in the general case can be
    easily reduced to this special case.) Hence $R=S\{z_1,\dots,z_r\}$
    (\cref{lem:III.9-frame-completion}). We shall prove the assertion of the theorem by
    induction on $a$. For $a=1$, the assertion is clear from the definition of a regular
    system of $\tau$-parameters of $R$ for $J$ (\cref{def:III.7}). Assume that the assertion is
    verified for a certain $a\ge1$. By the completeness of $R$, if
    $S_a=S\{z_{\tau_a+1},\dots,z_r\}$, then $(S_a;z_1,\dots,z_{\tau_a})$ is a regular frame of
    $R$. By the induction assumption, the initial forms of $f_1,\dots,f_{m_a}$ in
    $\operatorname{gr}_M(R)$ belong to the associated $k$-subalgebra of
    $(S_a;z_1,\dots,z_{\tau_a})$ (\cref{def:III.9-associated-subalgebra}). We can easily see
    that if $j$ is any integer such that $1\le j\le m_{a+1}-m_a$ then
    $(f_1,\dots,f_{m_a},f_{m_a+j})$ can be extended to a standard base of $J$. Moreover, as is
    easily seen, $f_{m_a+j}$ is normalized by $(f_1,\dots,f_{m_a})$ with respect to
    $(S;z_1,\dots,z_r)$ and therefore, in view of Remarks 1 and 2 (\cref{rem:III.7-1},
    \cref{rem:III.7-2}), $f_{m_a+j}$ is normalized by $(f_1,\dots,f_{m_a})$ with respect to
    $(S_a;z_1,\dots,z_{\tau_a})$. Therefore, by Lemma~19 (\cref{lem:III.19}), the initial form
    of $f_{m_a+j}$ $(1\le j\le m_{a+1}-m_a)$ in $\operatorname{gr}_M(R)$ belongs to the
    $k$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{gr}_M(R)$ generated by the initial forms of
    $z_1,\dots,z_{\tau_{a+1}}$. \qed

    \textbf{Formalization (the printed route).} The reduction to the
    complete case is the base change of \S8 for the identity $S\to S$
    (\texttt{RegularFrame.baseChangeHom}, $\hat R=S\{z_1,\dots,z_r\}$): the hypotheses transfer
    (regular $\tau$-frame, \texttt{RegularFrame.isRegularTauFrame\_of\_map}; standard base,
    \texttt{isStandardBase\_iff\_isStandardBase\_map}; normalization,
    \texttt{RegularFrame.isNormalizedBy\_baseChangeHom}; $\nu^*$, $t$, $\mu$, $\tau$ unchanged,
    \texttt{tauStar\_map}), and the conclusion descends
    (\texttt{initialForm\_mem\_framePrefixSubalgebra\_of\_map}). In $\hat R$ the induction on $a$
    is carried out with the partial frames $(S_a;z_1,\dots,z_{\tau_a})$
    (\texttt{RegularFrame.partialFrame}), Remarks~1 and~2 for them
    (\texttt{RegularFrame.isNormalizedBy\_partialFrame}) and Lemma~19
    (\texttt{initialForm\_mem\_adjoin\_of\_isNormalizedStandardBase\_mvPowerSeries}).

    \textbf{Gaps in the paper filled.} (1) The reduction to the complete case is not carried
    out in the paper. (2) For $a=1$ (``clear from the definition'') the same step as for the other
    $a$ is used, Lemma~19 for the empty system. (3) ``We can easily see'' that
    $(f_1,\dots,f_{m_a},f_{m_a+j})$ can be extended to a standard base: the greedy selection
    (\texttt{extendsToStandardBase\_snoc}). (4) That $T^*$ of Lemma~19, generated by a regular
    system of $(a+1)$-th $\tau$-parameters and $Z_1,\dots,Z_{\tau_a}$, lies in
    $k[Z_1,\dots,Z_{\tau_{a+1}}]$: the system $(z_1,\dots,z_{\tau_{a+1}})$ is one
    (\texttt{isRegularSystemOfTauParameters\_prefix}). -/)
  (latexEnv := "theorem")]
theorem initialForm_mem_adjoin_of_isNormalizedStandardBase [Hironaka.HironakaCitedResults.{u}] (F : RegularFrame R) (J : Ideal R)
    (hF : F.IsRegularTauFrame J) {m : ℕ} (f : Fin m → R)
    (hf : F.IsNormalizedStandardBase J f)
    (a : ℕ) (ha : 1 ≤ a) (hat : a ≤ t R J)
    (ma : ℕ+) (hma : IsGreatest {n : ℕ+ | nuI R J n = (mu R J a : ℕ∞)} ma) :
    ∀ j : Fin m, (j : ℕ) < (ma : ℕ) →
      initialForm (maximalIdeal R) (f j) ∈
        Algebra.adjoin (R ⧸ maximalIdeal R)
          (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin F.r // (l : ℕ) < tau R J a} => frameForm F.z l.1) := by
  classical
  have ht1 : 1 ≤ t R J := ha.trans hat
  -- "`R` may be assumed to be complete": the base change for the identity `S → S`, `R̂ = S⟦z⟧`
  set a₀ : F.S →+* F.S := RingHom.id F.S with ha₀def
  have ha₀ : RingHom.MapsRSOP a₀ := RingHom.mapsRSOP_id F.S
  have hsepa : RingHom.IsResiduallySeparableAlgebraic a₀ :=
    RingHom.isResiduallySeparableAlgebraic_of_residueField_surjective (by
      intro c
      obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := IsLocalRing.residue_surjective c
      exact ⟨IsLocalRing.residue F.S s, by rw [ResidueField.map_residue]; rfl⟩)
  set α := F.baseChangeHom a₀ with hαdef
  have hα : RingHom.MapsRSOP α := F.mapsRSOP_baseChangeHom a₀ ha₀
  have hsepα : RingHom.IsResiduallySeparableAlgebraic α :=
    F.isResiduallySeparableAlgebraic_baseChangeHom a₀ hsepa
  have hsepα' : RingHom.IsResiduallySeparable α := hsepα.isResiduallySeparable
  -- the hypotheses hold for `R̂`
  have hfR : ∀ j, initialForm (maximalIdeal R) (f j) ∈ Set.range (frameAlgHom F.z) := fun j => by
    have h := hf.2.1 j
    unfold RegularFrame.assocSubalgebra Hironaka.assocSubalgebra at h
    rwa [Algebra.adjoin_range_eq_range_aeval] at h
  have hf' : (RegularFrame.mvPowerSeries F.S F.r).IsNormalizedStandardBase (J.map α)
      (fun j => α (f j)) := by
    refine ⟨(isStandardBase_iff_isStandardBase_map α hα J f).mp hf.1, fun j => ?_,
      fun j => F.isNormalizedBy_baseChangeHom ha₀ _ (fun l => hfR _) (f j) (hf.2.2 j)⟩
    obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := hfR j
    rw [initialForm_map_of_mapsRSOP α hα, ← hq,
      grMapMax_frameAlgHom α hα F.z (F.baseChange F.S).z
        (fun l => (F.baseChangeHom_z' a₀ l).symm) q]
    unfold RegularFrame.assocSubalgebra Hironaka.assocSubalgebra
    rw [Algebra.adjoin_range_eq_range_aeval]
    exact ⟨_, rfl⟩
  have hF' : (RegularFrame.mvPowerSeries F.S F.r).IsRegularTauFrame (J.map α) :=
    RegularFrame.isRegularTauFrame_of_map α hα hsepα' F _ J ht1 rfl
      (fun j => (F.baseChangeHom_z' a₀ j).symm) hF
  obtain ⟨htα, hτα, -⟩ := tauStar_map α hα hsepα' J
  have hnuI : ∀ n, nuI _ (J.map α) n = nuI R J n := fun n =>
    (nuI_map_eq_of_mapsRSOP α hα J n).symm
  have hnu : nuStar _ (J.map α) = nuStar R J := (nuStar_map_eq_of_mapsRSOP α hα J).symm
  have hmu : mu _ (J.map α) a = mu R J a := mu_congr_of_nuStar_eq hnu a
  have hma' : IsGreatest {n : ℕ+ | nuI _ (J.map α) n = (mu _ (J.map α) a : ℕ∞)} ma := by
    simpa only [hnuI, hmu] using hma
  -- the complete case
  have key := initialForm_mem_adjoin_of_isNormalizedStandardBase_mvPowerSeries (J.map α) hF'
    (fun j => α (f j)) hf' a ha (by rw [htα]; exact hat) ma hma'
  intro j hj
  have h1 := key j hj
  have hτa : tau _ (J.map α) a = tau R J a := hτα a ha hat
  rw [hτa] at h1
  -- the conclusion descends
  exact initialForm_mem_framePrefixSubalgebra_of_map α hα hsepα' F.z F.z_injective F.extends_rsop
    (RegularFrame.mvPowerSeries F.S F.r).z (RegularFrame.mvPowerSeries F.S F.r).z_injective
    (RegularFrame.mvPowerSeries F.S F.r).extends_rsop (fun l => (F.baseChangeHom_z' a₀ l).symm)
    (tau R J a) (f j) h1

end Theorem7

end Hironaka
